<concept id="t00162">
	<title id="e00840">Service interval </title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00841">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00842">
								<image href="images/OCL4M035116C.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e00843">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Service in</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>The vehicle calculates and displays when you need a scheduled maintenance service (based on mileage or days).</p>
		<p>If the remaining mileage or time reaches 1,500 km (900 miles) or 30 days, the “Service Interval” message displays for several seconds each time you turn the <term translate="no">ENGINE START/STOP</term> button to the <term translate="no">ON</term> position.</p>
	</conbody>
